<DocSection Title="Using it in your own application">
    <p>
        The modules, packages and components of the framework are open-source components. They stay so when they are
        installed in, or run from, an application or a hosting environment that a customer owns.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Installing them does not transfer their ownership.</li>
        <li>Installing them does not limit the customer's right to use them under the licence.</li>
        <li>
            The customer owns the host application, the code, design, configuration, integrations and business logic
            written specifically for it, and its data.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        A project created with the <code>dotnet new</code> templates is yours, and so is the mapping code that
        ShiftMapper generates in it. Neither needs attribution. The packages they reference keep their own licences.
    </p>
</DocSection>

<DocSection Title="This page and the licence">
    <p>
        This page explains the licence and does not change it. If you have a signed agreement with Shift Software,
        that agreement prevails over this page.
    </p>
</DocSection>
